State the worker setting in force, and keep the language box while it loads

A run reported "4/4 workers" with 8 configured. Every code path that reads the setting looked
correct, so rather than guess, the value in force is now stated: the log gets
"SubSync worker limit is N (configured: M, ceiling: 64)" whenever it changes, and the run line
adds "setting is M" whenever the configured value disagrees with the limit being used. One line
then settles it.

The language box also keeps its own options while the subtitle lists are read - it is disabled and
the word plus the real count appear inside it ("LOADING 45/280") instead of replacing its contents
with a placeholder, which made the control look like something else.

Version 1.1.0.36.
